# The test corpus, counted. A later sweep diffs against this file.
#
# baseline: 1afc0ae637fac88b61281498d4044a311231e4d7
# taken: unrecorded
#
# Columns are `tier scope count`. `gdunit` scopes are directories and
# their counts are `func test_*` read from the source, because a suite
# that fails to parse emits no XML and a run cannot see it. `hosted`
# and `module` scopes are family tags. The `all` scope on a run tier is
# what that run actually discovered. It exceeds the source total by the
# parameterized expansions and falls short of it by whatever failed to
# parse, so a move in either direction is worth reading.
#
# Regenerate with `.agents/bin/test-census --write`. This file is
# crossing infrastructure and is deleted with `tests/crossing/` once
# `ledger carried-shell` reads 0 and every ledger has closed.
#
# `ledger` scopes count crossing-ledger rows by disposition. `carried`
# splits into `carried-kit`, what stays GdUnit forever under the argued
# permanent set, `carried-shell`, what a Ring-0 subject still owes a
# re-authoring, and `carried-retiring`, whose subject the campaign
# DELETES and which closes with the unit its token names.
# `carried-shell` and `carried-retiring` both reaching 0 is what closes
# the ledgers and
# retires this file. `carried-unclassed` is the count the gate refuses on
# and must read 0.

